"""## Question Time 🤔

What is the skew value representing here??

What does it mean if my skew value is very negative or very positive or what if it is zero??

---

## Your Answer:

Skew Value is a measure of how asymmetric our distribution is in comparison with the ideal symmetric bell curve.
1. Skew = 0 -> distribution is symmetrical (Perfect Skewness)
2. Skew > 0 -> right-skewed; long tail of the graph stretches to the right and Mean > Median > Mode (Positive Skewness)
3. Skew < 0 -> left-skewed; long tail stretches to the left and Mean < Median < Mode (Negative Skewness)

-> A more detailed evaluation of the magnitude can be:
- Around 0 -> nearly symmetric.
- Between [–0.5, 0.5] -> fairly symmetric.
- Between [–1, –0.5] OR [0.5, 1] -> moderately skewed.
- Less than –1 OR greater than 1 -> highly skewed.

#### In the Age KDE Plot above, skewness = 0.39 hence data is fairly symmetric, with the tail slightly stretching on the positive side as some passengers were really old.
---
"""

